  "about": "Where Bambu Lab publishes each AMS firmware image. OpenAMS stores no Bambu firmware: an image is either downloaded from url (Bambu's public download server) or imported from the Bambu offline package named in package (bambulab.com > Support > Firmware download), then checked (size, MD5, BIMH header, inner_name) before the bridge sends it. family uses OpenAMS names (ams1, ams2 = AMS 2 Pro, ams_ht). hardware is the board revision the image is built for. source is the printer release that carries it.",
